  "body": "The G-code viewer now lists every program line from the left edge, and a line wider than the window stays on its one row.\n\n### What was wrong\n\n- `pages::gcode_listing` drew each line with `ui.add_sized([width, row_h], Label)`. egui lays that widget out in a centred-and-justified layout, so every line's text was centred in its row. On `main` 8f30bee, in the test program below, `M30` is painted at x 273 and the motion line above it at x 159.\n- The same layout let a line wider than the window wrap onto a second row (30 px against a 15 px row). Every row below it was then off the scroll-cursor arithmetic, which divides by one fixed row height.\n\n### What changed\n\n- Each row is a left-to-right box exactly the listing's width and one monospace row tall (`allocate_ui_with_layout` plus `set_min_size`). The text starts at the left edge, and the row height is unchanged, so the cursor law (the clip rect's middle row is the published line) holds as before.\n- A line wider than the window is truncated on its row, and egui shows the whole line on hover.\n- Syntax colouring, the issue's second (\"see about\") ask, is not in this PR. It needs new per-word text colours that pass the contrast law on both built-in themes and every colour-vision mode, and maybe new theme-file keys, so I've left a proposal on the issue for the owner. Hence `Refs`, not `Fixes`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/256-gcode-left-align.md` (`Label::halign` inside `add_sized`, and a horizontal scroll bar, were considered and dropped).\n\n### Tests (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/gcode_viewer.rs`, through the real shell layout)\n\n- `every_gcode_line_starts_at_the_listings_left_edge`: `%`, `M30` and a long motion line are painted at the same x. It reads the painted text shapes from the frame output, because the accessibility rect is the row's box and spans the row either way.\n- `a_line_wider_than_the_viewer_stays_on_one_row`: a 120-character comment is one row tall and starts at the same left edge.\n- With `pages.rs` put back to `main` (`git stash` of that file only), both fail: \"`M30` starts at x 273, the longer motion line at x 159\", and \"the wide comment is 30 tall, a one-line row 15.125\". The two existing viewer tests (`the_viewer_window_publishes_the_scroll_cursor`, `a_successful_post_opens_the_viewer_and_new_document_retires_it`) pass with the change.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local, built from upstream `main` 8f30bee plus this commit)\n\n- The quick gate's plan for this diff (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -DryRun`, run by hand with `-j 3` because another session was using most of the CPU): ui lib plus `boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `theme_files`. 283 pass, 2 ignored, 3 fail.\n- The 3 failures are the UI pixel snapshots (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`, `tool_editor_snapshot`). They fail on clean `main` on this machine by the same pixel counts (1544, 1815, 2080; #255). The viewer is closed in every snapshot, so this change can't move them.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not run: the windowed app by hand, Linux, macOS.\n\nChangelog: The G-code viewer lists program lines from the left edge instead of centring them, and a line wider than the window stays on one row (#256)\n\nRefs #256\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
